# DraftPolicy-1 (lane DraftPolicy, 2026-10-31; HuntDrafter F10): TF_GLM_DRAFT_EDGE, the DFlash2 chain's selector edge
# weight (dflash2.EDGE, the recipe's 0.6, fitted on 9 dumps) as a knob. Refit offline with draft_sim on the 24 real
# agent turns' TF_GLM_DRAFT_DUMP records (work/hunt/DraftPolicy/REPORT.md), held out by turn: EDGE 0.2 with
# DRAFT_POLICY=fcost7:noisy +1.8% (greedy) / +1.7% (sampled proxy) decode tok/s at P1 over fnc7:0.3; with fnc7:0.3
# kept, +1.1% / +1.0%. Unset or empty: 0.6, the same float: picks, confidences and replies bit-identical to the base.
# Any value: replies identical by construction (drafts are verified); only which drafts a round proposes changes.
# Read once at import on every rank (start.sh passes every TF_GLM_* to every rank); the engine's startup settings
# comparison now carries it, so ranks given different values refuse to start instead of proposing different drafts.
# draft_dump records it in each dump's meta (``edge``), which draft_sim's check already reads.
# Test: work/hunt/DraftPolicy/test_draft_edge.py (CPU); mutants: mutants.py (7 of 7 killed).
# Applies with `patch -p0` in the folder holding tensorfold/, at the end of stack/all6t.list.
--- tensorfold/families/glm5_next/cuda/dflash2.py
